      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Hey Tupper, I've experienced this issue and its difficult to reproduce due to how it happens, but from testing it appears to most commonly happen if you and the person you have blocked loads into the world at the same time. \nThe person being blocked will some times be able to see the person who has them blocked. This happens in my experience when someone drops a portal in a world and everyone in the instance migrates, and if you happen to load into the new instance roughly the same time as the other person, this has a chance to happen. \nI'll keep in mind to save my logs if I notice it happening again, though from my own experience looking at them I haven't noticed anything informative for this particular issue. \nThis should be reproducible if you replicate the conditions of 2 people joining an instance at the same time multiple times until it happens. I am not certain which of the pair of individuals needs to join first, but you can just have both individuals testing block each other, and replicate the above conditions. A person who is blocked cannot see the person who blocked them in the user list, but the converse is not true, so you can use that to see when the bug happens.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
